SUMMARY:[Natural Language Processing & LLMs][Deep Representation Learning] 
 IJCNLP 2026 - ARR paper submission deadline
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: Asia-Pacific ACL and International Joint Conf
 erence on Natural Language Processing\nWebsite: https://2026.aaclnet.org/
 \nSource URL: https://2026.aaclnet.org/calls/main_conference_papers/\nLoc
 ation: Hengqin\, China\nTopics: Natural Language Processing & LLMs\, Deep
  Representation Learning\, LLM Agents & Tool Use\, Information Retrieval 
 & Search\nSize: L\nSubmission type: Paper-based\nConfidence: confirmed\nL
 ast checked date: 2026-10-07\nNotes: Joint AACL-IJCNLP 2026 is one editio
 n under the IJCNLP series\, not two conferences. ARR submissions and both
  commitment rounds are closed. Joint-series recurrence is irregular\; do 
 not automatically invent an annual next edition. Size is an editorial est
 imate.\nScope: Computational linguistics and natural-language technologie
 s in the Asia-Pacific community\, including multilingual and low-resource
  NLP\, language modeling\, generation\, dialogue\, structured prediction\
 , and evaluation. The 2026 edition is jointly organized as AACL-IJCNLP. A
 lias identity is preserved without inheriting the separate ACL conference
  ranking.\nAdditional topics: Cognitive Science & Computational Cognition
 \, Explainability & Interpretability\, Fairness & Responsible AI\, Human-
 AI Interaction & Deployment\nScope sources (2026): https://2026.aaclnet.o
 rg/calls/main_conference_papers/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
